---
title: "JRN-006 Exception Path EX-001 — Down-Valuation"
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    actor PER001 as PER-001<br/>Personal Customer
    participant Channel as Channel<br/>Customer Portal / App (CAP-007)
    participant CAP001 as CAP-001 API<br/>Retail Banking
    participant EB as Event Bus<br/>SVC-102
    participant Surveyor as External Surveyor<br/>(Drive-By)

    Note over PER001,Surveyor: Entry: PH-012 Valuation<br/>Preconditions: Full application submitted, hard credit check passed<br/>Property: £390,000 | Loan: £292,500 | Deposit: £97,500 | LTV: 75%

    rect rgb(255, 248, 220)
        Note over CAP001,Surveyor: PH-012 — Valuation Instructed (drive-by: LTV >= 75%)
        Note over CAP001: Determine valuation type: drive-by (LTV=75% triggers surveyor)<br/>Create ENT-014 PropertyValuation (status: instructed, type: drive_by)<br/>Transition status: valuation_pending
        CAP001->>EB: Publish EVT-024 ValuationInstructed { application_id, type: drive_by }
        CAP001->>Surveyor: Instruct drive-by survey (SLA: 2–3 business days)
        Note over Surveyor: 2 business days: surveyor conducts drive-by inspection
        Surveyor-->>CAP001: Valuation report: £355,000 (vs purchase price £390,000)
    end

    rect rgb(255, 200, 200)
        Note over CAP001,EB: DOWN-VALUATION DETECTED
        Note over CAP001: Update ENT-014 PropertyValuation:<br/>valuation_amount: £355,000 | down_valuation_flag: TRUE<br/>Recalculate LTV: £292,500 / £355,000 = 82.39%<br/>Exceeds product limit (max 80%)<br/>Transition status: valuation_complete
        CAP001->>EB: Publish EVT-025 ValuationCompleted<br/>{ application_id, amount: 355000,<br/>down_valuation: true, ltv: 82.39 }
        Note over EB: Route EVT-025 (down_valuation: true) → Notifications (SVC-053):<br/>Email to customer: Down-valuation notification<br/>Surveyor value: £355,000 vs purchase: £390,000<br/>Options: 1) Renegotiate price  2) Increase deposit  3) Withdraw<br/>Respond within 28 days
    end

    rect rgb(255, 248, 200)
        Note over PER001,CAP001: Customer selects Option 2: Increase deposit by £35,000
        Note over PER001: Customer reviews with solicitor.<br/>Decides to increase deposit to maintain purchase price.
        PER001->>Channel: Select: Increase deposit by £35,000<br/>New deposit: £132,500 | New loan: £257,500
        Channel->>CAP001: PATCH /mortgage-applications/{id}<br/>{ deposit_amount: 132500, loan_amount: 257500 }
        Note over CAP001: Update ENT-012 MortgageApplication:<br/>deposit_amount: £132,500 | loan_amount: £257,500<br/>ltv_ratio: £257,500 / £355,000 = 72.54% (within 80% limit)<br/>Recalculate monthly payment at new loan amount
        CAP001-->>Channel: 200 OK { ltv: 72.54, status: proceeding_to_underwriting }
        Channel-->>PER001: Application updated. Proceeding to underwriting.
    end

    rect rgb(230, 255, 230)
        Note over CAP001,EB: PH-013 — Underwriting (amended application)
        Note over CAP001: Transition status: underwriting<br/>PER-055 assigned — notified of down-valuation history<br/>PER-055 review:<br/>Loan: £257,500 | LTV: 72.54% PASS<br/>Affordability (stress 7%): PASS<br/>Credit score: 715 PASS<br/>Down-valuation: resolved (deposit increased) PASS<br/>Decision: APPROVE
        CAP001->>EB: Publish EVT-026 MortgageUnderwritingCompleted<br/>{ application_id, decision: approved, loan_amount: 257500 }
        Note over PER001,Surveyor: Journey continues on happy path → PH-014 Mortgage Offer (£257,500)
    end

    Note over PER001,Surveyor: Alternative resolutions (not shown):<br/>Option A: Renegotiate price to £355,000 → same end state, different deposit/price ratio<br/>Option B: Withdraw → application status = withdrawn, no further processing
